Fillets: a blend rolling on an edge (an obstacle, 0011) whose other
contact changes faces on the way while the ball goes on rolling on the
same edge (mitcad#121): e.g. the edges between the sides of a plate with
round corners and a bevel along its bottom narrower than the rounding;
the ball touches the side and rolls on the bevel's bottom edge, and where
the side turns into a corner (a cylinder as round as the ball) the
contact passes onto the corner while the ball rolls on along the bevel's
edge (at the corner the ball's centre stays put: the blend is a part of
the ball).

ChFi3d_FilDS: each SurfData puts the point where it ends on an arc into
the arc's interferences, which cuts the edge there. Where a SurfData
rolling on an edge ends at an inner point of that edge because its other
contact reached the end of its face, and the next one rolls on from
there on the same edge, that point cut the obstacle edge between the two
pieces of the blend that run along it; the piece of the edge beyond the
point then came twice into the wire of the face across the edge (the
edge's piece and the next blend's contact curve along it), and the face
was invalid (BRepCheck_UnorientableShape). Such a point (RollsOnAcross:
not a vertex, on the obstacle edge of both SurfDatas) no longer cuts the
edge; the edge is cut at its vertices, where the ball passes onto the
next edge, as before.
